  "narrative": "Synthesis at this point integrates the returned validation evidence with the current discovery evidence.  \n\nFirst, H11, the feature_058 main effect within the feature_036 low tail, is now definitively unsupported as a threshold-exceeding dataset association. Its discovery estimate was +0.156 signed units with 95% interval +0.012 to +0.300 (R12): the point estimate slightly exceeded the 0.15-unit threshold, but the interval did not support a threshold-exceeding effect with confidence. The independent validation estimate is +0.107, validation interval -0.118 to +0.332 (R23). The validation point estimate is below the threshold and the validation interval includes both no association and effects below the threshold. Taken together, discovery and validation are more consistent with a weak or null association than with a meaningful effect. I therefore reject and close H11. This also leaves the broader feature_058/feature_036 tail line closed.\n\nSecond, H34, the main feature_010=1 versus feature_010=0 weaker-dependency/higher-outcome association, is now strongly supported by both discovery and independent validation. Discovery gave +0.423 composite dependency-score units with 95% CI +0.327 to +0.520 (R20). The independent validation estimate is +0.421 with validation-adjusted interval +0.293 to +0.549 (R50). Both intervals have lower bounds well above the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed positive direction. I accept and close the exact H34 claim. Interpretation remains limited to dataset association: feature_010=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 values, meaning weaker composite dependency relative to feature_010=0. The validation result strengthens the internal reliability of this dataset finding, but it is not a causal claim and does not guarantee generalization beyond these samples.\n\nTogether with the previously validated H19 finding, this gives two clear dataset-internal association axes. feature_037=1 is strongly associated with much stronger dependency: discovery signed +0.833 (R21) and validation signed +0.800 (R37). feature_010=1 is robustly associated with weaker dependency/higher score: validated +0.421 (R50). The stratum analyses for these axes are broadly concordant: feature_037 remains very large within feature_010 strata and across feature_040 and feature_019 splits, while feature_010 remains positive across feature_037, feature_040 low, and feature_019 strata. The one weaker subgroup is high feature_040 H56, where the feature_010 point estimate is +0.290 but the lower confidence bound is +0.068 (R41), below the threshold. I therefore close that exact subgroup claim as unresolved: the broader feature_010 main effect is validated, but subgroup-specific threshold evidence in that stratum is not established.\n\nA new high-priority line is feature_002. The original H21 exact dependency-increasing claim was rejected because the signed estimate was large and opposite: -0.832 (R48). The reversed main claim H70, feature_002=1 versus 0 in the higher-outcome/weaker-dependency direction, is supported by the same evidence with signed estimate +0.832, 95% CI +0.766 to +0.897 (R48). This is far above the 0.15-unit threshold and the interval is very tight. I therefore accept H70 as a dataset-internal association while keeping its investigation active. The essential next question is independence from the already accepted feature_037 and feature_010 axes. The registered feature_002 stratum claims within feature_037=0, feature_010=0, and their joint baseline, plus the newly proposed feature_037=1 and feature_010=1 strata, will test whether feature_002 remains associated when conditioning on these other strong predictors. Persistence would support an additional robust dataset axis; attenuation or disappearance would make it more likely that feature_002 is correlated with, proxying, or entangled with the accepted axes rather than being an independent association. Independent validation should be considered for feature_002 after the conditional evidence clarifies this.\n\nNegative findings continue to accumulate. The named binary research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 do not support main dependency-increasing effects, and the feature_058/feature_036 tail line is now closed after failed validation. The feature_003 main line is closed because discovery +0.141 (R18) and validation +0.119 (R36) are below the threshold. Several binary screens are also unsupported or below threshold, including feature_048, feature_023, feature_031, feature_047, feature_016, feature_013, feature_024, feature_041, feature_001, and feature_035. These negatives do not prove universal absence of association, but they reduce the plausibility that many common measured binary variables in this dataset have large threshold-exceeding marginal effects on the composite dependency score.\n\nThe most informative next work is to run the feature_002 conditional analyses and then decide whether H70 deserves independent validation. The two newly proposed feature_002 stratum contrasts within feature_037=1 and feature_010=1 complement the existing zero-stratum tests and will help distinguish an independent weaker-dependency association from correlation with the accepted axes. After that, the most useful remaining discovery work is a focused continuation of untested binary screens, but feature_002 follow-up should dominate analysis slots because it is the newest large, robust discovery signal. Broad exploration should continue at lower priority, while avoiding low-yield feature_036-tail and feature_003 lines unless a new strong non-tail signal appears.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 4 synthesize updates.\n\nCore supported dataset associations:\n- feature_037 dependency-increasing: H19 accepted and closed after discovery +0.833 (R21) and validation +0.800 (R37). Robust across feature_040 and feature_019 strata and feature_010 conditioning.\n- feature_010 weaker-dependency/higher-outcome: H34 now accepted and closed after discovery +0.423 (R20) and validation +0.421 (R50). Validation interval +0.293/+0.549, lower bound >0.15. Exact main claim closed.\n- feature_002 weaker-dependency/higher-outcome reversal: H70 accepted active based on signed +0.832 CI +0.766/+0.897 (R48). Not yet validated. Need conditional independence tests versus feature_037 and feature_010.\n\nConditional/independence plan:\n- H71 feature_002 within feature_037=0.\n- H72 feature_002 within feature_010=0.\n- H73 feature_002 within feature_037=0 and feature_010=0.\n- New: feature_002 within feature_037=1 and within feature_010=1.\nInterpretation: persistence in zero strata/joint baseline supports separate axis; attenuation in conditioned strata suggests correlation/proxy. Validation candidate after conditional results.\n\nClosed negative lines:\n- H11 feature_058 low feature_036 tail rejected after validation +0.107 interval -0.118/+0.332 (R23); discovery R12 also not threshold-supported by lower bound.\n- feature_003 closed: discovery +0.141 (R18), validation +0.119 (R36).\n- H56 high feature_040 feature_010 subgroup: unresolved/closed exact subgroup because point +0.290 but lower bound +0.068 below threshold (R41); does not threaten validated main H34.\n- feature_048, feature_023, feature_031 rejected/closed based on R46/R47/R49.\n- Prior markers and common binary screens remain rejected/closed.\n\nNext analysis priorities:\n1. Run feature_002 conditional claims (H71-H73 plus new feature_037=1 and feature_010=1 strata).\n2. If feature_002 persists conditionally, request validation of H70 or its best main representation.\n3. Continue moderate broad binary/categorical screens only after feature_002 line resolved.\n4. Do not spend resources on feature_036 tail, feature_003, or weak near-threshold screens unless new evidence changes priority."
